<title>POLAND: NBP clears Commerzbank stake rise in BRE.</title>
<headline>NBP clears Commerzbank stake rise in BRE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland, the central bank, cleared German Commerzbank's plan to raise its stake in the Polish Bank Rozwoju Exportu to 32.9 percent from the current 21 percent, BRE said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the central bank's decision was binding until the end of 1997. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Earlier on Friday Commerzbank said that it would seek to raise its stake through acquisitions of existing shares rather than newly-created ones, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>The Polish Securities Commision (KPW) said on Thursday it had approved an acquisition of up to 11.9 percent of BRE by Commerzbank, a deal which would take the German bank's stake up to 32.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
